ssion. If the expression cannot be evaluated, the formula has an error instead of a value, never both {value xor error}.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A formula depends on the cells referenced by its expression (CellReference and Range). The reflexive association on Cell records that. It is derived from the expression (marked with /) and kept so that after an edit only the dependents are recomputed, and a formula that reaches its own cell is rejected as a circular dependency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The arguments of a FunctionCall are expressions (numbers, cell references, operations, other function calls) or ranges. A Range covers all the cells between upperLeft and bottomRight and is not an Expression, so it can only appear as an argument. A single cell is written as a CellReference, which as an argument behaves like a Range whose two corners are the same cell.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In an S2V file the ';' between function arguments is written as ','." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;size=18;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="930" y="340" width="440" height="320" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>